  "notes": "Historical catalog year, built for the parallel per-year build-out (see docs/BRANCH_CAMPUS_FINDINGS.md for methodology). Fetched the real archived 2023-24 bulletin page (bulletins.psu.edu/archive/2023-2024/undergraduate/colleges/health-human-development/hospitality-management-bs/) and parsed its raw HTML 'sc_plangrid' table row-by-row via BeautifulSoup rather than trusting an AI summary -- each semester's item credits were checked to sum to that semester's own printed subtotal (e.g. Second Year Fall's own stated '15-17' matches HM 230(3) + HM 235-or-ACCTG 211(3-4) + HM 265-alt(3) + HM Elective(3) + STAT-alt(3-4)) before being trusted. Real, confirmed differences from the 2025-26/2026-27 sequence, found by diffing the full course-code list scraped from this archive against later years: (1) TWO separate First-Year-Seminar credits are required ('PSU First-Year Seminar' 1cr AND 'HM 297S' 1cr), not the single 1-2cr FYS slot later years use -- modeled as an added explicit HM 297S item alongside the existing FYS slot (net +1 credit vs. the 2025-26/2026-27 template). (2) Three real alternative-course choices existed that later years dropped entirely: 'ECON 102 or 104' (Sem 1 Spring), 'HM 272 or MIS 250' (Sem 1 Spring, MIS 250 an Information Systems course), and 'HM 355 or BA 243' (Sem 1 Spring). All three collapsed to their single first-listed course by 2024-25. (3) The organizational-behavior requirement was a three-way choice -- 'HM 265, MGMT 301, or BA 304' -- not the single dedicated course HM 265W that 2024-25 introduced; modeled per the flowchart's literal text (see the item's own inline note on the HM 265/HM 365 inconsistency within this SAME archived page). (4) 'STAT 100, 200, or SCM 200' -- an extra SCM 200 (Supply Chain Management) alternative not offered by 2024-25 onward. SCM 200's own real prereq is MATH 21 (never in this plan), so the engine will simply never actually pick it over STAT 100/200 -- included for a faithful options list, not because it's a live path. (5) HM 290W (Hospitality Managerial Communication) was still a separately required course (same finding as HM-2024.json), not yet folded into a generic elective. (6) NUTR 100 or 251 alternative (Third Year Spring) -- 251 dropped by 2024-25. (7) Plain 'CAS 100' was still a listed alternative alongside 100A/100B/100C (dropped from the live page's text by 2026-27, though CAS 100 the base course still exists in the catalog). Confirmed IDENTICAL across this year and all later years: HM 101/202/203/230/242/280/330/336/350/366/430/ 480/492 and their semester placement, ENGL 15/30H/ESL 15, ENGL 202A-D, HM 271, credit totals for every unchanged semester. Retained the same two catalog-driven fixes already documented in HM-2026.json's own notes, since hm_catalog.json's course descriptions/prereqs are shared across every catalog year in this app: the explicit 'HM 201' item in Semester 5 (HM 366's real prereq, which this year's flowchart -- unlike 2022's -- never lists on its own) and the HM 490->HM 490W substitution (HM 492's real prereq is HM 430 AND HM 490W; the 2023-24 flowchart, like every other year, literally prints plain 'HM 490'). Added MGMT, BA, MIS, and SCM to 'departments' since this year's real alternative courses live in those departments' own catalogs -- all four confirmed to exist with real credits/prereqs in this app's already-scraped mgmt_catalog.json/ ba_catalog.json/mis_catalog.json/scm_catalog.json (checked directly, not assumed). Campus availability: the 2023-24 archive's own campus toggle reads identically to every other year checked -- End Campus 'University Park' only; Erie (Behrend) and Brandywine are not offered for this program.",
